  "content": {
    "title": "Happy Pi Day! Here’s where to get the best deals in 2026",
    "text": "Whether you prefer your pie sweet or savory, or just in decimal form, Pi Day 2026 features a lineup of deals from national chains offering free or discounted slices of the pie all day.Pi Day falls on March 14 every year, and this year it falls on a Saturday. We did the math so you don’t have to. Here are the latest deals for this Pi Day. Go with your family or divide and conquer to get all the deals this year.7-Eleven/Speedway/Stripes7-Eleven is extending its Pi Day observance to two days.Participating locations are dishing up oven-baked pizzas, quesadillas and cinnamon-sugar pies for $3.14 each for rewards members.Blaze PizzaAt Blaze, guests can purchase one 11-inch pizza and get a second of equal or lesser value for $3.14 at participating locations. This marks the chain’s 13th year of Pi Day celebrations.It’s not stopping there. Those who visit on March 14 will receive a digital code for a buy-one-get-one-free 11-inch pizza.“Pi Day is more than a promotion for us, it’s a celebration our fans look forward to every year,” Casey Terrell, chief marketing officer at Blaze Pizza, shared. “It’s our way of saying thank you to the guests who have made Blaze part of their traditions. Whether you’re a longtime fan or visiting for the first time, this $3.14 deal is the perfect excuse to grab a friend and enjoy your favorite custom-built pizzas together.”Burger KingBurger King is wrapping up a weeklong promotion that helped customers navigate the first week of daylight saving time. To claim the Pi Day freebie — a Hershey’s or cinnamon apple pie — guests just need to make a qualifying purchase of $3.14 or more, per Snackolator.Marco’s PizzaMarco’s is offering a medium one-topping pizza for $3.14 with the purchase of a large or extra-large pizza. Customers can order online via Marco’s Pizza’s site or app and use the promo code PIDAY at checkout, according to The Food Network.Mountain Mike’sWhen guests at the family-style pizza eatery purchase any medium pizza at regular price, they can snag another medium pizza for just $3.14 on March 14, according to Mountain Mike’s.Mountain Mike’s Pizza celebrates Pi Day: Buy one medium pizza, get a second medium one-topping pizza for $3.14. | Mountain Mike’s Pizza via Business WireCrumblThe cookie-centered dessert chain is dishing up pie this Pi Day, but staying true to its cookie roots, with a cookie dough pie. The pie has a “brown sugar and graham pie crust nestling a cookie dough-packed brown sugar cream cheese filling, topped with fresh whipped cream, more cookie dough pieces and mini chocolate chips,” Crumbl says.The special pie is available all week long, and for those who go on March 14, each Crumbl location will offer its own surprise bonus pie flavor to celebrate the holiday.Marie Callender’sThe restaurant bakery is offering guests a slice of pie for $3.14 on Pi Day.DoorDashThe food delivery service is offering nationwide Pi Day offers from three pizza chains, according to the Food Network:Pizza Hut: When customers order one medium or large create your own pizza from participating locations, they can get one free on March 14.Sbarro: Customers can get $4 off eligible orders of $20 or more from all participating locations from March 14 through April 6. DashPass members can get $5 off eligible orders of $25 or more.Blaze Pizza: From March 14 through April 6, when customers buy one “Simple Pie” 11-inch cheese pizza, they get one free when they order from participating locations.",
